{
  "description": "Identifiers and plain names for the place pages (roadmap R360). sameAs links each place to the Wikidata item that carries its GSS code. A plain name drops the ONS suffix (\", City of\", \", County of\") from the title, the H1 and the breadcrumb only; the page URL, the area code and every figure are unchanged.",
  "wikidata": {
    "publisher": "Wikidata",
    "endpoint": "https://query.wikidata.org/sparql",
    "query": "SELECT ?code ?item ?itemLabel (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?inst; separator=\"|\") AS ?insts) WHERE { VALUES ?code { <the 318 area codes in src/data/live/ethnic-projections.json> } ?item wdt:P836 ?code . OPTIONAL { ?item wdt:P31 ?inst } SERVICE wikibase:label { bd:serviceParam wikibase:language \"en\". } } GROUP BY ?code ?item ?itemLabel",
    "rule": "The item whose GSS code (property P836) equals the area code. Isle of Anglesey (W06000001) has two such items, the island and the principal area; the principal area (instance of Q15979307, as for the other 21 Welsh areas) is used.",
    "accessed": "2026-11-04"
  },
